This factorial function uses itself.

```python
def fact(n):
    if n == 0:
        return 1
    return n * fact(n - 1)
```

Each pill is one call of `fact`. A line from one call to the next means "calls".

The same idea adds up a list of daily P&L figures.

```python
def sum_list(xs):
    if not xs:
        return 0
    return xs[0] + sum_list(xs[1:])
```

`xs[1:]` is the list without its first item.

The call that answers without calling again is the **base case**. The line that calls on a smaller input is the **recursive case**. This version stops at one item instead:

```python
def sum_list(xs):
    if len(xs) == 1:
        return xs[0]
    return xs[0] + sum_list(xs[1:])
```

